 * `token=` goes on by hand instead of through `searchParams`: the CLI listener
 * reads the token straight out of the query without percent-decoding it, so a
 * re-encoded `/` or `=` would reach it as a token the auth API rejects. Both
 * characters are legal in a query string as they are.
